         /// capacity for the event
+        /// ZAY-LOCAL-PATCH: upstream blocks the caller forever once the queue
+        /// is full. When the UI thread wedges mid-handler (it drains events
+        /// while holding the queue mutex), the input thread parks here
+        /// permanently — every key silently vanishes while the app keeps
+        /// showing its last frame. Bound the wait instead: retry tryPush for
+        /// ~2s, then drop the event with a visible warn. A TUI must lose one
+        /// input event, never its whole input thread.
